  "year": 2024,
  "arxivId": "2402.03300",
  "abstract": "DeepSeekMath is a domain-specific language model that significantly outperforms the mathematical capabilities of open-source models and approaches the performance level of GPT-4 on academic benchmarks. It achieves this through a combination of large-scale math pre-training, mathematical instruction tuning, and an efficient reinforcement learning algorithm called Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO).",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "DeepSeekMath aims to improve mathematical reasoning in language models by leveraging large-scale math pre-training and efficient reinforcement learning. The key insight is that <strong>high-quality math pre-training data</strong> can significantly enhance the model's mathematical reasoning capabilities. The authors introduce the DeepSeekMath Corpus, a large-scale dataset of 120B math-related tokens sourced from Common Crawl.",
